overview=dict(status='usable',rationale='Representative formation, authority transition, old-work handling and necessary membership/recovery/application support have been traced. Local discrepancies and deeper variants remain explicitly open.',formation=path('The elected leader stamps and persists commands, then reports its local match and notifies peer replicators. Sender-bounded AppendEntries and snapshot success report matching indexes to a tenure-local commitment object, which includes only latest-configuration voters. Its majority order statistic advances only through the current-term startIndex. A main-loop notification consumes that index, commits membership and enqueues ordered FSM work; follower append handling propagates leader commitment after prefix checks and conflict replacement. runFSM resolves command futures after callbacks, while log dispatch watermarks precede callback completion.','B-replicate B-quorum B-commit-consume B-fsm','F-quorum-index','M-apply M-commit M-send M-reply M-update M-follower M-leader-loop M-fsm M-fsm-rest'),context=path('Normal timeout candidacy requires local voter eligibility. Optional pre-vote precedes term persistence, self-vote and requests only to voters. Recipients enforce candidate membership, term, prior vote and last-log freshness; request-specific response channels and majority tally acquire leadership. Transfers catch up a target then send TimeoutNow, whose election bypasses pre-vote/known-leader rejection but still tallies votes. Incoming qualifying terms, higher-term replication replies, lease loss and committed self-removal end a tenure. Old replication callbacks retain old commitment/stepDown objects; cleanup stops workers, fails remaining inflight/verification futures and discards tenure fields. Already queued FSM work can still complete. Network heartbeat fast-path carries no entries or commitment and may run concurrently.','B-election B-tenure B-transfer B-transport B-verify-start B-verify-support B-verify-finish','F-verify-support','M-election M-vote M-elect-send M-leader M-leader-loop M-transfer M-timeout-now M-lease M-net-dispatch'),connection=path('Persistent vote/term and log freshness constrain subsequent authority acquisition; durable log entries survive tenure loss although their uncommitted futures fail. Each new leader resets volatile match evidence and appends a current-term noop before advancing old-history commitment. Configuration admission waits for both stable membership and current-term commitment, then changes the support electorate; suffix replacement can roll latest membership back. Snapshot capture includes applied history plus committed configuration, and restart/install reconstruct history and membership before participation/catch-up. Verification is a separate authority-support path: its threshold counts voters, but notification registration spans all replicators. That discrepancy is retained without equating callback count with legitimate authority.','B-election B-tenure B-membership B-history B-resync B-quorum B-verify-start B-verify-support','F-quorum-index F-verify-support','M-durable M-restart M-snapshot-build M-install M-snapshot-send M-commit M-leader M-verify M-notify'),core_gaps=[],open_details=['Verification eligibility and callback timing relative to election/lease expiry.','Legal sender history for follower commitment beyond the current validated request prefix.','Partial-store-error recovery after conflict truncation; delayed snapshots; manual Restore and forced RecoverCluster paths.','Transport-specific pipeline ordering and error behavior beyond representative dispatch.'])
